  "reason": "Rejected: the v5 canary has clean binary transparency, correct N/S topology, and continuous four-neighbor seams, but its alpha>=240 (and total visible, because alpha is binary) perpendicular widths are N 23/22/21 px and S 24/24/17 px at the 50/75/100% samples, below the required 36-42 px complete ribbon and below the 28 px loam core at every sample. Its longitudinal overflow is 15.65 px N and 12.07 px S, exceeding the 8 px limit, so both ends remain too long and the S terminal pinches. Heartlands verge richness is also materially thinner than the approved straight-EW reference.",
